{
author: "SlideDeckML"
title: "Reusable Components Demo"
theme: "black"
transition: "slide"
}

@component arrayDisplay values highlight
:::{ position: absolute; top: 100px; left: 100px; width: 600px; background: #1e1e1e; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; }
# Array Visualization
${values}
:::{ background: #ffeb3b; color: #000; padding: 5px; border-radius: 5px; }
Highlighted element: ${highlight}
:::
:::
@end

@component stepCard number title content
:::{ background: #667eea; padding: 30px; border-radius: 15px; margin: 20px; }
### Step ${number}: ${title}
${content}
:::
@end

===

# Sorting Algorithms Lecture

Welcome to our interactive demonstration of sorting algorithms using reusable components!

===

## Bubble Sort - Initial State

@use arrayDisplay values="[5, 2, 8, 1, 9]" highlight="5"

Below we see the unsorted array with the first element highlighted.

===

## Bubble Sort - After First Pass

@use arrayDisplay values="[2, 5, 1, 8, 9]" highlight="9"

After the first pass, the largest element (9) has bubbled to the end.

===

## Code Example: Bubble Sort

This is the complete implementation of bubble sort algorithm.

===

## Quick Sort - Initial Array

@use arrayDisplay values="[7, 3, 9, 2, 5]" highlight="7"

The pivot element (7) is selected for partitioning.

===

## Algorithm Steps

@use stepCard number="1" title="Choose Pivot" content="Select the first element as the pivot"

@use stepCard number="2" title="Partition" content="Rearrange elements smaller than pivot to the left, larger to the right"

@use stepCard number="3" title="Recursion" content="Recursively apply the same process to sub-arrays"

===

## Code Example: Quick Sort

A recursive approach to sorting.

===

## Merge Sort - Divide Phase

@use arrayDisplay values="[8, 3, 5, 4]" highlight="8"

The array is divided into smaller sub-arrays.

===

## Multiple Arrays Comparison

Comparing sorted sub-arrays before merging.

===

## Performance Analysis

@use stepCard number="1" title="Bubble Sort" content="Time Complexity: O(n²) - Good for small datasets"

@use stepCard number="2" title="Quick Sort" content="Time Complexity: O(n log n) - Fastest on average"

@use stepCard number="3" title="Merge Sort" content="Time Complexity: O(n log n) - Stable and predictable"

===


